 "rule": "A set is a balanced design: a table of factor rows (procedure kind, scope, number of instrument exchanges, assistant instrument, smoke), fixed below. Each row gets one 63-bit seed from os.urandom, in table order; the hidden set's rows are then put in an order drawn from os.urandom as well. No draw is ever rejected or repeated: nothing about a drawn procedure (how the reference or anything else scores on it) decides whether it is kept. Everything the factors do not pin (the cavity, the sites and the path, the gestures and their timing, when an exchange happens, every look) follows from the seed (endosim/procedure.py). The file records, for every procedure, the generator's facts and two render-free measurements made after the draw: what a holder that never moves scores, and what the reference scores (tests/review/fast_eval.py's loop). They are a record, not a filter.",
